  "market_context": "The market had just completed a strong initial impulse move (Wick-to-Wick top to bottom), followed by a pullback into the Fibonacci retracement zone. The analyst emphasized this as the highest-probability setup for continuation entries.",
  "key_observation": "A massive engulfing candle formed precisely within the 0.382–0.618 Fibonacci retracement zone after the initial impulse, serving as a clear rejection signal for a trend continuation trade.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identify the initial impulse move from swing low to swing high, measured Wick-to-Wick.",
    "Step 2: Draw Fibonacci retracement levels (0.382, 0.5, 0.618) from that impulse move.",
    "Step 3: Wait for price to retrace into the 0.382–0.618 zone—the key rejection area.",
    "Step 4: Observe a massive engulfing candle forming in that zone, confirming rejection and signaling a long entry."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "The strongest continuation entries occur when price retraces into the 0.382–0.618 Fib zone and produces a decisive rejection pattern like an engulfing candle—this confluence increases probability significantly.",
